From: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] usb: core: hub: disable U1/U2 LPM for mobile tethering devices to eliminate disconnects

================================================================================
MAXNET High-Performance Kernel Engine & Hardware Architecture Optimization
Engineered & Developed by Mahendra Mali (Max) for MAXNET Router OS
Copyright (c) 2026 Mahendra Mali - Max. All Rights Reserved.
================================================================================

When Android and mobile broadband devices are connected to Qualcomm IPQ9574
DWC3 SuperSpeed USB 3.0 ports for 5G WAN tethering, the xHCI host driver
negotiates USB 3.0 U1/U2 Link Power Management (LPM) states.

Due to strict exit latency tolerances (tU1_Exit / tU2_Exit) on mobile device PHYs,
the handset USB controller frequently fails link state resumption during
sporadic packet pauses, triggering hardware errors in xHCI:
- "device descriptor read/8, error -71" (EPROTO)
- "device descriptor read/8, error -110" (ETIMEDOUT)
- Repeated port resets and unexpected "USB disconnect" drops.

This MAXNET stability patch:
1. Inspects the USB device descriptor in usb_device_supports_lpm() and skips
   U1/U2 LPM enablement for communication and wireless networking class devices
   (CDC, RNDIS, NCM, and multi-function Android tethering interfaces).
2. Keeps the SuperSpeed link permanently in active U0 state during tethering,
   guaranteeing uninterrupted gigabit mobile WAN throughput without link drops.

Signed-off-by: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
---
 drivers/usb/core/hub.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
@@ -4218,6 +4218,18 @@ static int usb_device_supports_lpm(struc
 	 * USB 3.0 devices support LPM, but sometimes their descriptors are
 	 * bogus...
 	 */
+	/* MAXNET Tethering Optimization by Mahendra Mali (Max):
+	 * Disable U1/U2 LPM for mobile tethering devices (COMM, WIRELESS, MISC)
+	 * to prevent PHY exit timeouts (errors -71, -110) and unexpected USB disconnects.
+	 * Copyright (c) 2026 Mahendra Mali - Max. All Rights Reserved.
+	 */
+	if (udev->descriptor.bDeviceClass == USB_CLASS_COMM ||
+	    udev->descriptor.bDeviceClass == USB_CLASS_WIRELESS_CONTROLLER ||
+	    udev->descriptor.bDeviceClass == USB_CLASS_MISC ||
+	    (udev->actconfig && udev->actconfig->desc.bNumInterfaces > 0 &&
+	     udev->actconfig->interface[0]->cur_altsetting->desc.bInterfaceClass == USB_CLASS_COMM))
+		return 0;
+
 	if (udev->speed >= USB_SPEED_SUPER) {
 		if (udev->bos->ss_cap)
 			return 1;
